      "attrs": {
        "text": "You are fixing a Critical bug in `src/server/storage/cli_db.py` (Talium code-econ storage module). Work from `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ`. Canonical interpreter: **`venv/bin/python`**.\n\n## The bug\n`main()` wraps `parser.parse_args(argv)` in `try/except SystemExit: return 1`. This catches argparse's `SystemExit(0)` for `-h`/`--help` too, so `main([\"--help\"])` returns 1 instead of 0. `--help` must exit 0 by CLI convention; invalid args (argparse exits 2) and unknown verbs must still return 1.\n\n## The fix\nChange the `except SystemExit: return 1` handler to branch on the exit code:\n```python\n    except SystemExit as e:\n        return 0 if e.code in (0, None) else 1\n```\n(argparse `--help` → code 0 → return 0; parse errors → code 2 → return 1). Change ONLY this handler in `cli_db.py`. Do not touch anything else.\n\n## Add a covering test\nIn `tests/server/storage/test_cli_db.py`, add:\n```python\ndef test_help_exits_zero(capsys):\n    assert cli_db.main([\"--help\"]) == 0\n```\nKeep the existing tests (`test_unknown_verb_returns_error_code` → 1, `test_import_reports_deferred` → 1) passing.\n\n## Verify & commit\nRun `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/test_cli_db.py -v` — all 3 tests pass (help→0, bogus→1, import→1). Also `venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/server/storage/ -q` (no regressions). Commit: `fix(storage): --help exits 0, not 1 (branch on SystemExit code)`.\n\n## Constraints\nNo \"Claude\" anywhere.\n\n## Report\nAppend to `/Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-10-report.md` under \"## Fix round 2\": the change, the test result. Reply with ONLY: Status, commit SHA + subject, one-line test result, report path.",
